* text=auto
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.lock text eol=lf
*.jsx text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
# Shell scripts and checksum sidecars are missing from the list above, so with
# `core.autocrlf=true` a Windows checkout gives them CRLF.  For a `.sh` that is
# not cosmetic: the kernel reads the shebang as `/bin/bash\r` and the script
# fails with "bad interpreter".  For a `.sha256` it silently changes the bytes.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.sha256 text eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
